info.description:
HTTP API for Redis and Valkey: standalone, cluster and sentinel.

Every JSON response is wrapped into Response; errors use ErrorResponse with a stable error_code.

Common query parameters (where they make sense):
db - database (standalone and sentinel);
node - send the request to the node with this address;
target - auto (by key), node, masters, replicas, all or sentinels; fan-out targets return a result per node;
encoding - auto (binary strings become {"base64": "..."}), utf8 or base64;
key_encoding=base64 - keys, fields and members in the query string are base64;
timeout - request timeout for blocking commands, e.g. 30s;
duration - duration of streams, exports and imports;
pretty - indented JSON.

In request bodies keys and values are strings, numbers or {"base64": "..."} objects.
